    [Doc] Correct context parallel guides and diagram labels (#19432)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Align the context parallel guides with the current implementation:
    
    - Document PCP connector requirements and DSpark SFA support, and fix
    DCP wording and localized anchors while preserving the compatibility
    matrices.
    - Correct the developer guide's DCP index/cache descriptions and KVPP
    TP×PCP ownership and PCP support.
    - Remove redundant model-runner version qualifiers and runner-selection
    exports from the guides and launch examples.
    - Correct labels in the existing DCP PNGs. Image dimensions and pixels
    outside the edited label regions are unchanged.
    
    Chinese translations are handled by CI; this PR does not modify `.po`
    files.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Documentation only; no runtime behavior changes or release note
    fragment.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `git rebase --force-rebase upstream/main` and `git rebase
    upstream/main`: passed. Verified a single PR commit with no merge
    commits and document/image contents identical to the reviewed version.
    - English documentation: `python -m mkdocs build --strict` passed.
    - `python -m pytest --noconftest -q
    tests/ut/_tools/test_generate_zh_docs.py`: 7 passed.
    - Markdownlint passed for the three changed English Markdown files; `git
    diff upstream/main --check` passed.
    - Checked local article links and images on the three affected English
    pages: no broken links. Verified that compatibility matrices are
    unchanged and PNG edits are confined to the intended label regions.
    - Local `bash format.sh ci` could not initialize because of Windows
    Schannel credentials. The [CI Run pre-commit
    step](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/39921392979/job/120307214981)
    passed on this commit.
    - No new runtime tests or NPU runs: implementation behavior was checked
    by source inspection, and this PR changes documentation only.
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    The runtime testing items below do not apply to this documentation-only
    change; documentation checks are recorded above.
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [ ] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: Added applicable runtime
    boundary tests.
    - [ ] **Regression test**: Added a runtime regression test.
    - [ ] **Error / failure path coverage**: Added runtime failure-path
    tests.
    - [ ] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: Added new behavior tests.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: Attached benchmarks for
    performance-sensitive changes.
    
